{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 3, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Upon the break of dawn, thou shalt arise and make thy way to the airport, where thy journey to Japan doth begin. Take a plane that doth fly across the sea, and gaze upon the vast expanse of water and sky from thy window seat.\n\nUpon arrival in Tokyo, the capital city, thou shalt rest and recover from thy journey.\n\nThe following day, visit the Meiji Shrine, a place of great reverence and beauty. Pay thy respects to the deities enshrined there, and marvel at the towering torii gates and serene forest surroundings.\n\nNext, explore the bustling streets of Harajuku and Shibuya, where thou shalt find unique fashion, delicious street food, and lively entertainment.\n\nOn the third day, venture to Nikko, a city nestled in the mountains north of Tokyo. Here, thou shalt find the Toshogu Shrine, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and the final resting place of Tokugawa Ieyasu, the founder of the Tokugawa shogunate.\n\nThe following day, return to Tokyo and visit the historic Asakusa district, where thou shalt find the Sensoji Temple, Tokyo's oldest temple.\n\nOn the fifth day, travel to Hakone, a hot spring resort town located in the Fuji-Hakone-Izu National Park. Here, thou shalt find beautiful views of Mount Fuji, as well as opportunities to soak in the healing waters of the hot springs.\n\nThe following day, return to Tokyo and spend thy final day exploring the city's many museums, parks, and gardens.\n\nAnd so, at the end of thy journey, thou shalt return home, filled with memories and experiences that shall last a lifetime. Farewell, and may good fortune follow thee on thy travels.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Upon", "logprob": -0.3254517912864685}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.020623529329895973}, {"token": "break", "logprob": -1.5643638372421265}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": "dawn", "logprob": -0.12775583565235138